1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,746
Lake Ridge Bancorp's third quarter:
earnings up twenty-six percent, but

2
00:00:04,746 --> 00:00:07,308
costs still run above its Wisconsin
peers.

3
00:00:07,858 --> 00:00:12,864
Earnings were four dollars
ninety-seven cents a share, up
twenty-six percent from a year ago.

4
00:00:12,864 --> 00:00:16,910
No analyst covers this stock, so there
is no estimate to compare with.

5
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:23,100
Revenue rose almost seventeen
percent to thirty-three and a half
million dollars. That was second

6
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,250
fastest of four Wisconsin banks.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:32,017
The efficiency ratio improved almost
three points, to about sixty-three
percent. But that is still the highest

8
00:00:32,017 --> 00:00:35,375
cost ratio of the four, where the
median is fifty-five.

9
00:00:35,925 --> 00:00:42,393
Credit got better. Nonperforming
loans fell to zero point two six percent
of loans, from zero point four seven

10
00:00:42,393 --> 00:00:44,080
at the end of last year.

11
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:50,801
Three things moved earnings from a
year ago. Net interest income added
three point six million dollars. Higher

12
00:00:50,801 --> 00:00:55,793
expenses took back two point two
million. And fee income added one
point one million.

13
00:00:56,343 --> 00:01:01,557
Watch three things next quarter.
Whether costs keep growing slower
than revenue. How rates move book

14
00:01:01,557 --> 00:01:07,075
value, which fell almost four dollars a
share in the quarter. And whether
problem loans keep falling.

15
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:13,359
The Madison bank is growing fast.
The question is whether it can close
the cost gap with its peers.

